# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# Avatar 30 fps base with frame generation x2 (60 fps displayed), -src 30, b:flip present, -lock -lag 75 -dejit. One benchmark test, no fade at either end. keep-real collapses each pair to its real member, so the policy sees 30 real frames into a 60 Hz sink and alternates one real frame with one midpoint blend, exactly as the FG-off 30 fps pair does.
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description Avatar 30 fps base with frame generation x2 (60 fps displayed), -src 30, b:flip present, -lock -lag 75 -dejit. One benchmark test, no fade at either end. keep-real collapses each pair to its real member, so the policy sees 30 real frames into a 60 Hz sink and alternates one real frame with one midpoint blend, exactly as the FG-off 30 fps pair does.
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
